`.github/workflows/linux.yml`, job `debian`:

    apt-get install -y --no-recommends libgit2-dev pkg-config git
    ...
    env:
      ALIEN_INSTALL_TYPE: system
    run: cpanm -nq Alien::Libgit2

The comment above the matrix still reads: "Alien::Libgit2 handed a system libgit2 by
pkg-config. On bookworm that is 1.5.1, which is the floor this distribution supports."

That floor moved. `cpanfile` requires `Alien::Libgit2 0.002`, and 0.002 raised the
system-libgit2 floor from 1.5 to 1.9.3 (Alien::Libgit2 0.002, Changes: "Raise the
system-libgit2 floor from 1.5 to 1.9.3 ... A system lib below the fix now falls through
to the bundled 1.9.3 share build."). Debian bookworm ships libgit2 1.5.1, so pkg-config
reports a version the Alien refuses.

`ALIEN_INSTALL_TYPE=system` does not fall back - it fails. Alien::Libgit2 0.002, POD
"Forcing an install path": "C<system> uses only a system libgit2 and fails if none meets
the floor". Bookworm's 1.5.1 does not meet 1.9.3, so the `debian` job cannot get past
`cpanm -nq Alien::Libgit2` - for all three perl versions of the matrix.

Alien::Libgit2 hit the same wall and fixed it in its own CI (0.002, Changes): "the linux
system-libgit2 job installs the bundled 1.9.3 into /usr/local instead of apt's
libgit2-dev. No Debian release reaches the floor (bookworm 1.5.1, trixie 1.9.0), so
since the raise that job had been falling through to a share build with none of the share
build's prerequisites installed." Copy that recipe here.

The `bundled` job (perl 5.40-bookworm, `ALIEN_INSTALL_TYPE: share`) and the macOS job
(Homebrew 1.9.4) are unaffected.

`README.md` states the same stale floor and belongs to the same fix:
- line 37: "**libgit2 1.5 is the floor.** All 236 bindings exist in 1.5.1."
- line 40: "prints which one a job took: 1.5.1 on perl 5.36/5.38/5.40 (Debian bookworm),
  the bundled 1.9.3 share build, and 1.9.4 from Homebrew on macOS."

Done when: the `debian` job installs a libgit2 >= 1.9.3 the way Alien::Libgit2's CI does,
the job comment names the real floor, and README states 1.9.3 instead of 1.5.

